<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Union Flag</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1801</span> · Also known as Union Jack</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Union Flag, or Union Jack, is the national flag of the United Kingdom. Its present form dates from 1 January 1801, when the red saltire of St Patrick, representing Ireland, was added to the crosses of St George for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and St Andrew for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, which had been combined on the flag since 1606.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/union-flag.jpg" alt="Union Flag" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Acts of Union 1800 Vector: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_(1-2).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
